# PR-7 allow-list (see xtask/src/strings.rs): string literals in the speech paths that are NOT
# user-facing messages: log and debug text, protocol names, attribute values, match patterns and
# internal ids. Format: `repo/path.rs | literal as written`; `repo/path.rs | *` allows a file.
# Adding a line here is a review decision: user-facing text belongs in the message catalog.
#
# Whole files: test-only modules (`#[cfg(test)] mod`), the presentation log (JSON keys), the
# daemon's command line and RT setup (developer-facing text on stderr, not speech) and the
# extension manifest parser (diagnostics for extension authors).
#
# Known gap, tracked for M14: settings and keymap diagnostics (compile.rs, config_task.rs) are read
# out by settings.report_problems in English; they quote paths and values. The rest below is not
# speech: log text, internal ids, match patterns, protocol names.
